BlitzView Portable — Licenses & Source

BlitzView is an open-source Qt6 media browser.
Copyright © 2026 Oliver Schmidt

This README describes the licenses for the software bundled in this
portable application. The full license texts are provided in the
subdirectories of this folder, one directory per bundled component.

BlitzView itself is free software, licensed under the GNU General
Public License version 3 (GPL-3.0-or-later). See BlitzView/GPL-3.0.txt.
Source code: https://github.com/blitzview-org/blitzview (project page: https://blitzview.org)

This portable build also bundles the following third-party components,
each under its own license (see the corresponding subdirectory for the
full text):

  Qt @QT_VERSION@ — GNU LGPL version 3          Qt/LGPL-3.0.txt
                     (the LGPLv3 incorporates the GPLv3 — its text is in
                      BlitzView/GPL-3.0.txt)
                     Source: https://download.qt.io/archive/qt/@QT_SERIES@/@QT_VERSION@/submodules/
  FFmpeg          — GNU LGPL version 2.1        FFmpeg/LGPL-2.1.txt
                     Bundled with the Qt binaries above, so the source is
                     part of the Qt source archive. Upstream:
                     https://ffmpeg.org/
                     Libraries in this package:
                     @FFMPEG_LIBS@
  MinGW/GCC runtime (libstdc++.dll, libgcc_s_seh.dll)
                     — GNU GPL v3 + GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1
                     mingw-runtime/GCC-RUNTIME-LIBRARY-EXCEPTION-3.1.txt
                     (base GPLv3 text: BlitzView/GPL-3.0.txt)
                     Source: https://gcc.gnu.org/ ,
                     https://github.com/AmanoTeam/mingw-gcc-cross
  MinGW-w64 runtime (linked into every executable and DLL here)
                     — Zope Public License 2.1, with parts in the Public
                       Domain / under BSD / LGPL
                     mingw-runtime/MINGW-W64-RUNTIME-COPYING.txt
                     Source: https://github.com/mingw-w64/mingw-w64
  MinGW-w64 winpthreads (libwinpthread.dll)
                     — MIT                       mingw-runtime/MIT-winpthreads.txt
                     Source: https://github.com/mingw-w64/mingw-w64/tree/master/mingw-w64-libraries/winpthreads

The Qt libraries and image-format plugins additionally contain code from
third-party projects (libjpeg-turbo, libpng, libtiff, libwebp, FreeType,
HarfBuzz, PCRE2, zlib, BLAKE2, md4c). Their licenses require their own
copyright notices to be reproduced: see Qt/THIRD-PARTY.txt.

In accordance with the GNU GPL and LGPL, the corresponding source
code for the GPL- and LGPL-licensed components is available from the
upstream locations listed above.

